<title>USA: MicroCap Fund directors resign.</title>
<headline>MicroCap Fund directors resign.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The MicroCap Fund Inc said three of its directors -- Jeffrey Lewis, Robert Naismith and Robert Tucker -- had resigned from its board as the fund continued to liquidate itself.</p>
<p>It said the remaining director, Raymond Troubh, who became chief executive officer in July, would oversee the liquidation of its assets.</p>
<p>In July, its shareholders approved a liquidation plan as MicroCap's primary activities had been limited to winding up its affairs.</p>
<p>MicroCap is a non-diversified, closed-end management investment company.</p>
</text>
